                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.6363/453: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cox</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-29T13:00:00-04:00">August 29, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>179. My 177, August 28, 5 p.m. Standard Oil Co. today tells me it has just signed
                    temporary agreement together with Shell-Mex which does not obligate companies to
                    accept marketing arrangement. Commission informs oil companies that final date
                    for their acceptance of the latter is September 22.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cox</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
